/* book: lead: A diode rectifier turns AC into pulsating DC using only the one-way conduction of a diode, so its average output is fixed by the supply peak and the circuit shape. Half-wave, centre-tap and bridge circuits are the three standard shapes, found at the front of almost every mains-powered supply. This chapter derives their average and RMS output, ripple factor, peak inverse voltage (PIV) and transform */
