/* book exam traps: Averaging the half-wave output over π instead of 2π. That gives 2Vm/π, the full-wave value; the half-wave average is Vm/π = 0.318 Vm. | Quoting the full-wave ripple factor 0.482 for a half-wave circuit, whose ripple factor is 1.21. | Giving the centre-tap PIV as Vm. It is 2Vm, the voltage across the whole secondary; the bridge diode sees Vm. | Using 230 V as Vm. For a 230 V rms supply, Vm = 230√2 = 325.3 V. | Calling TUF an efficiency. It compares Pdc with the transformer's VA rating. */
