/* book exam traps: Using 2f in the half-wave ripple formula. Half wave uses f; full wave uses 2f. | Saying the capacitor never changes the PIV. A half-wave circuit's PIV doubles to 2Vm. | Giving Vdc = 2Vm/π for a capacitor filter. That belongs to the choke-input filter; with C the output sits near Vm. | Treating a bigger capacitor as free improvement: it raises the peak diode current. */
